{"id":"G2043","lemma":"ἐρείδω","transliteration":"ereidō","sayIt":"ereidō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to immobilise","meaning":"ἐρείδω\n(chiefly in poets and late prose for ἐρυγγάνω), [in LXX for תָּמַךְ (Pro.4:4 5:5 11:16, al.), etc. ;]\nto prop, fix firmly: act., as mid., ἐρείσασα, of a ship driving ashore (RV, struck), Act.27:41.†\n(AS)","glosses":["stuck fast"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"act-27","v":41,"renderings":{"bsb":"stuck fast","kjv":"stuck fast"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Acts 27:41","note":"But coming to a place where two seas met, they ran the vessel aground. The bow struck and remained immovable, but the stern began to break up by the violence…","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20430","lemma":"ἐπίκυφος","transliteration":"epikuphos","gloss":"bent over, crooked"},{"id":"G20431","lemma":"ἐπιλαλέω","transliteration":"epilaleō","gloss":"be said of . ."},{"id":"G20432","lemma":"ἐπιλειόω","transliteration":"epileioō","gloss":"to shave"},{"id":"G20433","lemma":"ἐπιλήθω","transliteration":"epilēthō","gloss":"to forget"},{"id":"G20435","lemma":"ἐπιλυπέω","transliteration":"epilupeō","gloss":"be troubled at"},{"id":"G20436","lemma":"ἐπίμεικτος","transliteration":"epimeiktos","gloss":"in combination"},{"id":"G20437","lemma":"ἐπιμερίζω","transliteration":"epimerizō","gloss":"to enumerate"},{"id":"G20438","lemma":"ἐπιμεσόω","transliteration":"epimesoō","gloss":"be at the middle"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}